invariant: INV-13
file: srv_auth.c
catches: srv_auth_test
reason: a signer's refusal inside the flight returns CH_EINVAL again,
  the code that says nothing was sent, from a flight whose ServerHello
  already went out, so a caller that retries on CH_EINVAL retries a dead
  session. bin/srv_auth_test requires the refusal's code to be CH_EAUTH.

--- old
        ct_wipe(sig, cap);
        *sig_len = 0;
        *alert = ALERT_INTERNAL_ERROR;
        return CH_EAUTH;
--- new
        ct_wipe(sig, cap);
        *sig_len = 0;
        *alert = ALERT_INTERNAL_ERROR;
        return CH_EINVAL;
